# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Everything the suite, the coverage run and the tools generate. One
# directory rather than a list: the coverage settings in pyproject.toml write their data and HTML
# there, tests/run-tests.sh puts the coverage bootstrap and the bytecode
# cache there, and `make check` proves nothing escaped it.
.build/

# The names the same tools use when run by hand, outside the entry point.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.tox/
.nox/

# Packaging output
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
MANIFEST

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# xtm's own runtime files, in case a developer points XTM_CONFIG_DIR or
# XTM_STATE_DIR at the checkout while testing by hand.
#
# Anchored to the repository root with a leading slash. Unanchored, these
# would match at any depth and silently swallow every examples/*/config.yaml
# -- which is exactly what happened before the leading slashes were added.
/config.yaml
/config.yaml.lock
/current_profile.*

# Generated by the example runner when it hides PyYAML.
examples/*/.pyyaml-blocker/

# Saved code-review reports (creview output; generated, not source).
